# SQL migration linter (M10 unit 4). .githooks/pre-commit stanza 5 has invoked
# `sqlfluff lint` on staged migrations since it was written, but the tool was in
# neither this file nor any developer's PATH, so the stanza always took its
# "not installed" branch and had never linted a file. Declaring it here is what
# turns that gate on. Configured by the repo-root .sqlfluff, which carries the
# measured baseline (sqlfluff 4.3.0: 753 violations across 43 files, 0 parse
# failures) and a reason for every excluded rule.
# Floor is >= to match every other entry in this file; the EXACT version is
# pinned by the generated requirements-dev.txt lock, which is what CI installs
# and diffs, so a rule-retuning point release still cannot redden a no-change
# day without a reviewable lock diff.
sqlfluff>=4.3.0
